Repair the complete CommonJS source below and return a corrected complete source file. Export exactly `{ setHovered }`.

`setHovered(cards, cardId, hovered)` receives an array of card objects shaped as `{ id, label, accent }`. All three properties must be strings, IDs must be unique, `cardId` must be a string matching exactly one card, and `hovered` must be boolean. It must return cards in the original order as fresh objects. Only the matching card's `accent` changes: use `"highlight"` when hovered is true and `"normal"` otherwise. Nonmatching cards retain their accent. Neither the array nor any input card may be mutated. Throw `TypeError` for malformed values and `Error` for duplicate or missing IDs. An empty array is valid input but necessarily produces the missing-ID error.

```javascript
'use strict';

function setHovered(cards, cardId, hovered) {
  if (!Array.isArray(cards)) throw new TypeError('cards must be an array');
  if (typeof cardId !== 'string') throw new TypeError('cardId must be a string');
  if (typeof hovered !== 'boolean') throw new TypeError('hovered must be boolean');

  const seen = new Set();
  for (const card of cards) {
    if (!card || typeof card !== 'object' || Array.isArray(card)) {
      throw new TypeError('each card must be an object');
    }
    if (typeof card.id !== 'string' || typeof card.label !== 'string' || typeof card.accent !== 'string') {
      throw new TypeError('card fields must be strings');
    }
    if (seen.has(card.id)) throw new Error('duplicate card id');
    seen.add(card.id);
  }

  if (!seen.has(cardId)) throw new Error('card not found');
  return cards.map((card) => ({
    ...card,
    accent: card.id !== cardId ? (hovered ? 'highlight' : 'normal') : card.accent
  }));
}

module.exports = { setHovered };
```

